WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-DE

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.859
Hello and welcome back to Lam Rim.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.080
This is episode 9.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.320
I call it: "Visit to the Center of the Sun".

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.900
We talked about something as big and powerful

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:29.380
as an atomic bomb that you use to clean a ketchup stain off your shirt or blouse.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:35.879
And I'm not exaggerating.  I want you to think exactly like that.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.410
Imagine this:

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.240
Today is Independence Day here in America.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:53.600
We often have a picnic with the family then.
It's the height of summer,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:02.880
and American children are eating hot dogs or hamburgers and putting too much ketchup on them, and then some ketchup drips onto their shirts.  Imagine

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:13.200
that the mother sends this shirt or blouse out into the middle of the sun to be cleaned.  To

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.840
clean a small red ketchup droplet.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.380
I know it's a strange image,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.020
but I want you to imagine it this way.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:36.080
I don't know what else to compare it to.  No idea

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.980
.  Simply send a tiny object towards the center of the sun.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.120
Today we will visit the center of the sun.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:55.280
And I am pleased to announce that we have just reached the 3rd and final section of the Lam Rim,

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.360
the steps on the path to enlightenment.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.700
Now we move on to the Bodhisattva activities:

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:12.040
the thinking and actions of a Bodhisattva,

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:17.000
a person with the highest motive: @KYES BU CHEN PO, which means:

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.700
person with a high motive.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.280
Those of you who have been following this Lam Rim for 10 years

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.860
should be happy that you have persevered, and that I have persevered, until this final part!

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.580
We have reached the final part, the last third.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.360
Now, the mathematicians among you should be thinking: Geshe-la,

00:02:44.079 --> 00:02:46.529
you said earlier that we still have 25% to go.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.240
Why is this the last third then?

00:02:51.240 --> 00:03:02.500
And the answer is that Pabongka Rinpoche's treatment of the topics during the last two days of Lam Rim is too short.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:09.540
His presentation on meditation and seeing emptiness,

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.480
the last two of the 6 completions, is not very long.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.680
I don't know what happened.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.820
It's possible that his sponsor came to him and said, "There's only enough food for two more days!

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.860
Hurry up!"

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:31.140
It is possible that he received a mystical message from Tara.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:35.960
Or perhaps he had an appointment elsewhere.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:50.480
But if you ask me, Pabongka Rinpoche kept the last two parts shorter because Je Tsongkhapa had already covered them in his great Lam Rim,

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.600
the Great Book on the Stages of the Path to Enlightenment, the Lam Rim Chenmo.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:01.040
Tsongkhapa did it so brilliantly that I can practically imagine Pabongka Rinpoche saying: "

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.540
Guys, there really is no reason why I should teach this,

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:12.560
because Tsongkhapa has already taught it, and in an extraordinary way."

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.940
And there are many stories about how Tsongkhapa wrote these last two parts,

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.780
and I am pleased that we will be studying them together.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:29.260
So we will conclude this Lam Rim series with great teachings on meditation and emptiness.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:38.680
Therefore, this section about the stages on the path for people who have Bodhichitta,

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.440
for Bodhisattvas, is

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.020
not as long as it could be.  Let's

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.640
look at the Tibetan:

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.780
@ GSUM PA SKYES BU CHEN PO'I LAM GYI RIM PAR BLO SBYANG BA LA Let

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:57.820
us practice our heart in the stages of the path for people with high motivation,

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.520
for people who are Bodhisattvas.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.700
@THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO SEMS BSKYED KHO NAR BSTAN PA PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.500
We will cover the lifestyle of a Bodhisattva

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.560
in 3 different steps.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.440
1)

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.860
@ THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO If you want to enter the Bodhisattva path, there is only one way to get there.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.620
Specifically, by achieving a certain state of mind.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:29.660
If you want to attain enlightenment, if you want the chance to attain enlightenment,

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:36.260
if you want the chance to help the world, then there is only one way:
You must develop Bodhichitta.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:44.460
You must develop this desire to attain enlightenment in order to be able to help countless living beings.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.700
Let me explain "countless" to you:

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.500
Bodhichitta is directed towards countless living beings.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:06:00.540
It is not just aimed at all the people in your city, or all the people in your country, or all the people on this planet.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.920
Free yourself!

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.800
If you want to send the virus to the center of the sun, if you want to visit the center of the sun,

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:14.220
then free yourself from this concept that we are only working for all people on this planet.
We don't do that!

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:23.680
Free yourself from this concept that we only want to help all fish, birds, and land animals.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.840
We don't do that!  That's

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.620
not what this is about.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.560
We are talking about the entire universe!

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:39.300
Today we decide: I want to help every living thing in the entire universe!

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.540
Every single virus,

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.360
bacterium,

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.300
whale,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.640
every human being in the universe.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:58.980
Go out at night, in Sedona, or outside of Sedona, Rim Rock is even better,

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:03.340
and look at the stars and imagine it.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:20.640
So, 1) You cannot practice the lifestyle of a Bodhisattva if you do not extend your mind towards this goal.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.709
And when you actually experience it,
which requires some practice,

00:07:28.709 --> 00:07:30.850
when you actually send out your mind,

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:41.480
when you are actually able to develop Bodhichitta, then the things you have to do in this world are nothing!

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.780
They are nothing.  They are insignificant.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:51.380
Helping everyone in this world is nothing.
It's simple.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.640
@PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA means: Let me tell you about the advantages of thinking this way.  This is the first step.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.657
@BYANG CHUB TU SEMS BSKYED PA'I TSUL.  This is step 2.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.560
How do you achieve this breakthrough, this mental breakthrough?

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.180
How do you perceive an entire universe and all the beings within it,

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.800
and then develop love for them?
Is that even possible?

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.760
Is that even possible?
This is step 2.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.560
Step 3: @SEMS BSKYED NAS SPYOD PA LA SLOB TSUL LO

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:27.080
We will learn to act like a Bodhisattva.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:34.900
If you have developed this hope of becoming a Bodhisattva, then the question naturally arises:
What do I have to do practically now?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:41.300
How do I spend the hours of my day if I want to act like a Bodhisattva?

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.260
What should I do?

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.600
What does my daily schedule look like?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.200
Here comes the first point:

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:58.860
@DANG PO NI, DE LTAR SKYES BU CHUNG 'BRING GI SKABS SU NGES 'BYUNG GI BSAM PAS KUN NAS BSLANGS

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:08.340
After covering the stages on the path for people with low and medium motivation,

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:13.960
you should now at least feel

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.100
that this life is truly painful, truly a problem.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.580
The virus simply makes this clear.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.020
But that's how it's always been.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.940
There has always been a virus called death.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.280
This virus is new.  It's much smaller.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.340
But at least now we're all thinking about it.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.220
@ LHAG PA'I BSLAB PA GSUM LA 'BAD PAS

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.479
Then we should work on the 3 exceptional trainings:

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:45.360
Treat others kindly.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.140
Spend time in meditation.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:52.980
And strive to recognize that things do not come from themselves.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:59.540
@'BAD PAS RANG GCIG PUS THAR BA'I GO 'PHANG THOB TZAM DANG 'KHOR BA LAS LDOG TZAM 'BYUNG

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.960
You yourself can reach Nirvana

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.980
and leave the wheel of life

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:11.500
if you practice these attitudes.
That will be possible for you!

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.000
We've already taught you that, we're done with that.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.000
@ DE TZAM GYIS MI CHOG

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.347
But you must not stop there.  Do

00:10:18.347 --> 00:10:20.880
n't stop there.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.040
You can catch even bigger fish.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:30.980
Much, much bigger fish.  Don't stop there!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.680
@SPANG BYA THAMS CAD MA SPANGS

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:39.500
If you implement what I have taught you so far,

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.260
you will not cleanse your heart

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.560
of all the impurities that exist.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.240
@THOB BYA YON TAN THAMS CAD KYANG YONGS SU MA RDZOGS PAS

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:52.720
and you have not yet attained all those highest spiritual qualities

00:10:52.720 --> 00:10:54.120
that you can attain.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.680
@MA RDZOGS PAS Therefore

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:02.480
@RANG DON DANG, GZHAN DON YANG NYI TSE BA LAS MI 'BYUNG

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:08.320
@NYI TSE BA is a very disturbing word here.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.600
A very sad word.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:16.340
You can work on these paths I have taught you so far,

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.480
on all the meditations I have taught you so far,

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:25.120
but the amount of good you will achieve for yourself and others

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:29.040
will only be a tiny part of what you have to do.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.900
@NYI TSE BA means: It's only a tiny part of what you should be doing.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:43.520
And by the way: This word is most often used in Tibetan to describe hell on earth.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.900
That's very strange.  So there is

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.580
this great hell that people can end up in.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:56.840
But I also always think about people who have a car accident, and the car explodes and they go up in flames.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:02.945
In the scriptures this is called: @NYI TSI BA'I DMYAL BA,

00:12:02.945 --> 00:12:08.220
a little piece of hell on this level.
On this level of reality.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:13.080
So this term @NYI TSI BA means: only a tiny piece.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:17.780
And here he says: You want to help yourself and you want to help others?

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:22.420
Everything I've taught you in the last 10 years is @NYI TSI BA.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:30.160
It's just a tiny part of what you can do, and now we're ready for the big things.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:35.880
But Geshe-la, why did we spend 10 years with @NYI TSI BA, on the little things?

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.460
Why didn't we start with the more important things right away?

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:44.660
Because the little things are the ladder by which you reach the higher things.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:50.080
You cannot achieve the higher things if you do not do the other two parts.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:55.093
If you do not practice all the stages of Lam Rim in the correct order,

00:12:55.093 --> 00:12:58.460
you could never reach the Bodhisattva part.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.560
So you can't just say: I don't want that.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:10.260
It is part of the Bodhisattva's way of life to master the lower paths that led you to her.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.760
And you never discard them.
You simply outgrow them.

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:21.140
@MI 'BYUNG ZHING SLAR THEG CHEN LA GZHI NAS 'JUG DGOS LA

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:27.320
There is this concept in Buddhism:

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.320
once you are ready,

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.460
and once you have the appropriate preparation,

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.300
you should dive directly into the lifestyle of a Bodhisattva,

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:42.080
because if you don't, you will have to do it again anyway.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.749
Sooner or later you'll have to end up there.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.700
Perhaps this life is necessary.
Perhaps it will happen later in this life.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:57.780
Sometimes people come to me and say:
I want to take a break from this Dharma.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.960
I feel like I need a break.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:05.740
I have other things to do now.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.600
I have this big project at work, or I have to take care of this family matter,

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.600
and I need to take a break.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.400
I remember saying that to one of my teachers in India once.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.350
45 years ago.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:31.960
I said, "I need a break."
And he looked at me and said, "Okay, but you will come back."

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.120
You come back because there is no other way.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:44.300
You're coming back.  You come back to him because you have to come back to him.  Life will bring you back to him.

00:14:45.029 --> 00:14:47.929
Because that's life.
You need the Lam Rim.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.901
Life will always bring you back to Lam Rim.  Unless you die.

00:14:52.901 --> 00:14:55.680
And even then, it will eventually bring you back to him.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:02.600
@SLAR means: You have to come back.  @ SLAR THEG CHEN LA GZHI NAS

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:07.250
@ GZHI NAS means: You will waste a lot of time if you have to come back to him.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:12.780
So you might as well do it now, instead of having to come back later.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:17.360
The next picture

00:15:17.360 --> 00:15:24.060
shows something I want to do with you in this episode 9.

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:27.400
I call it "Visit to the Center of the Sun".

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.000
In this image

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:41.220
- I was looking for an image that roughly describes what it feels like to attain Bodhichitta -

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:42.520
so this image,

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:46.280
as we, Seiji and Tim, have noticed, looks
a bit New Age-like.

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:50.680
It looks like it was painted in Sedona, Arizona.

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:58.120
It feels a bit like New Age, but let me tell you: if you ever attain Bodhichitta,

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:00.870
then this is what it will feel like;

00:16:00.870 --> 00:16:10.660
the image is close.  Can you leave it standing?  Just one more minute.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:15.700
This picture isn't crazy, and it's not a hippie thing either.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:22.540
When you attain Bodhichitta, true Bodhichitta, it feels exactly like this.

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:28.040
Perhaps you would like to copy the image.
We've already paid for it.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:32.680
So you can use and store it at home.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:38.320
You should have such an image with you, perhaps as a screensaver or on your mobile phone.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:43.660
It comes pretty close to the feeling of attaining Bodhichitta.

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:49.600
I'd like to take you on a little trip, just for fun, maybe for 5 minutes.  Let

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:57.180
's revisit what it feels like

00:16:57.820 --> 00:17:03.100
when you first achieve true Bodhichitta.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:12.480
It is not about merely imagined or partial Bodhichitta.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:15.980
Or the attempt to feel as if you have Bodhichitta.  We're talking about the real issue here.

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:24.120
If one day you directly see emptiness and directly experience Bodhichitta,

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:27.340
we'll simply look at that experience,
because it brings happiness.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:30.340
It is an atomic bomb.

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:37.900
If you continue working on this feeling, on

00:17:38.180 --> 00:17:41.200
how it feels when you persevere,

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:43.780
then that will contribute to the destruction of the virus.

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:47.740
I believe this will help to destroy the virus.
It's like a nuclear weapon.

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:51.740
And the virus is like the ketchup stain.  Imagine

00:17:53.040 --> 00:18:03.140
, for just 5 minutes, what it feels like to achieve Bodhichitta.

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:07.620
Take 10 slow breaths.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:16.600
Focus on exhaling, a long exhale, don't worry about inhaling, your body will breathe.

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:53.640
Now please imagine that you have just seen emptiness directly.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:58.800
And now you come out of this direct perception

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:05.960
and return to what we can call normal meditation, which is still not back in this world.

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:11.640
You are in a deep state of meditation; you are still sitting on your cushion.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:15.060
Your eyes are closed.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:25.900
Then suddenly the image of your mother comes to mind.  It's your mother.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:36.500
A very, very perfect picture of your mom.  A living picture.  It really is your mother.  The way

00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:40.720
you remember her best.  That's exactly what

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:45.260
she looks like right now.  She's

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:51.140
looking at you.  She looks into your eyes.

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:58.700
Even though it feels like she's in the front part of your mind, she's looking into your eyes.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:10.260
With great love and also with an expression of distress.  She urgently needs help.  She's

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.440
in trouble.  It's like

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:25.320
she's jumping off the Titanic or something,
and she's looking at you with these eyes.
She says: I need you, I need help.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:42.560
Then you say aloud to her in your heart: "Don't worry, Mom, I'll take care of you."

00:21:45.140 --> 00:21:50.100
I will be strong enough to take care of you.  Do not worry.

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:59.080
I will have the strength to help you.
And I will do it, I promise.

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:16.200
Then her image fades before your mind's eye,
and suddenly there is the image of your father.  You

00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:19.500
see your father.

00:22:21.280 --> 00:22:31.260
He has the same expression in his eyes.
Anticipation.  But also anxious.

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:37.400
With a questioning look: "Can you help me?"

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:42.880
Things in life are hard, life has become difficult.

00:22:43.260 --> 00:22:47.360
You say, "Dad, don't worry. I'll take care of it!

00:22:47.820 --> 00:22:49.820
I'm studying the Lam Rim.

00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:54.120
I'm learning a lot about emptiness.

00:22:54.120 --> 00:23:01.280
And I know for sure that I'll have the tools to help you soon.

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:04.740
Don't worry. I'll take care of it."

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:09.540
Please - you don't need to be afraid.
You don't need to worry.

00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:13.380
I know what needs to be done: And I'm doing it!

00:23:13.820 --> 00:23:17.120
Everything will be alright, don't worry!

00:23:21.740 --> 00:23:29.700
Then perhaps an image of someone else in your life appears, someone close to you, your wife or husband or one of your children;

00:23:30.020 --> 00:23:33.280
the image of this person appears in your mind.

00:23:33.540 --> 00:23:35.540
Just her face.

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:44.940
She also looks at you and asks: "Can you help me? Things are bad, things are really bad!"

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:51.820
Things are deadly; there is no hope.  Can you help me?

00:23:54.220 --> 00:24:02.140
You say, "I've got this, I'll take care of it. I can do this!

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:07.920
I'll have enough strength to take care of you.

00:24:07.920 --> 00:24:10.020
You don't have to worry.

00:24:10.020 --> 00:24:11.800
I know what's going on.

00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:13.640
I understand your situation.

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:16.800
I know what this life is like.

00:24:17.020 --> 00:24:24.500
I get it, and I'm going to take complete care of you. Do

00:24:24.680 --> 00:24:28.640
n't worry. You really don't need to worry.

00:24:28.880 --> 00:24:31.540
I'll take care of it."

00:24:37.420 --> 00:24:43.320
Then that face fades, and then you can gradually imagine other faces of people you know.

00:24:46.000 --> 00:24:48.000
Close friends, family.

00:24:49.260 --> 00:24:51.260
Uncles and aunts.

00:24:51.680 --> 00:24:53.680
Brothers, sisters.

00:24:55.280 --> 00:24:57.280
Nephews and nieces.

00:24:59.300 --> 00:25:07.420
One by one, they appear, and you comfort them.

00:25:08.480 --> 00:25:15.260
You say, "I'm really going to take care of it."   "
You don't need to worry."

00:25:19.120 --> 00:25:22.400
In this way, you go through all the people you know

00:25:22.780 --> 00:25:26.100
and all the people you've ever met in your life.

00:25:26.480 --> 00:25:34.160
Then you start to consider all the people you haven't met yet and all the people in this world.

00:25:34.500 --> 00:25:37.000
Begin with your neighbors.

00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:45.820
Go through the whole city, and sure, you can't look at every single person.

00:25:46.440 --> 00:25:50.380
But take one person here and there.

00:25:50.940 --> 00:25:57.160
Extend that to the shores of the continent
you live on.

00:25:57.640 --> 00:26:00.240
Look at them all.

00:26:00.900 --> 00:26:03.500
Then go even further.

00:26:03.860 --> 00:26:06.460
To other continents.

00:26:07.920 --> 00:26:14.080
In this way, you reach all the people in the world.

00:26:15.920 --> 00:26:18.400
While you're still sitting here.

00:26:19.160 --> 00:26:23.820
Then you can begin with the animals of this world, with the fish.

00:26:24.920 --> 00:26:34.380
I'm not talking about specific species here:
I'm talking about helping every single animal.

00:26:36.500 --> 00:26:39.890
Each one is looking at you. Each one is expectant.

00:26:39.890 --> 00:26:44.260
Each one is afraid.
Each one receives your personal promise:

00:26:44.620 --> 00:26:47.700
"It's my turn."  “I’ll take care of it.”

00:26:48.760 --> 00:26:55.080
Imagine every single creature, tiny creatures at the bottom of the sea.

00:26:56.140 --> 00:26:59.120
Tiny living beings in your bloodstream.

00:26:59.780 --> 00:27:02.300
Meet each one.

00:27:03.100 --> 00:27:05.260
Talk to them.

00:27:05.720 --> 00:27:13.720
When you’ve finished with all the living things on this world, then start on the next world.

00:27:14.020 --> 00:27:17.280
I don’t know where the next world is. Alpha Centauri? It’s

00:27:17.660 --> 00:27:22.560
probably many light-years away.

00:27:24.040 --> 00:27:32.100
Go there and do the same meditation for everyone on that world.

00:27:34.060 --> 00:27:41.660
In this way, you reach all the worlds in the entire universe.

00:27:42.000 --> 00:27:51.740
And the karma of meeting 7 billion people, one by one,

00:27:52.840 --> 00:27:57.600
and trillions of other creatures, on one planet,

00:27:58.060 --> 00:28:04.640
and then on all the planets that exist,
countless planets,

00:28:04.640 --> 00:28:08.040
meeting all the beings there,

00:28:09.680 --> 00:28:11.680
that is Bodhichitta!

00:28:12.020 --> 00:28:15.820
That is the direct experience of Bodhichitta.

00:28:15.840 --> 00:28:24.340
If you can, in this episode,
simply develop this feeling,

00:28:26.140 --> 00:28:31.260
then you don’t have to worry about yourself.
You don’t have to worry about your family.

00:28:31.880 --> 00:28:35.080
You don’t have to worry about your country.

00:28:35.780 --> 00:28:40.740
And you don’t have to worry about a  A world overrun by the virus. These are small things!

00:28:41.720 --> 00:28:47.680
And we will take care of them too: because
we are working on a bigger project.

00:28:49.460 --> 00:28:54.820
We are working to help an entire universe!

00:28:55.920 --> 00:28:58.380
Countless billions of beings.

00:28:59.400 --> 00:29:03.560
Countless billions of animals and other creatures.

00:29:05.140 --> 00:29:10.680
We have this ability. You have this ability.
I pray that you may attain it in this lifetime.

00:29:11.240 --> 00:29:14.760
I pray that you may awaken it in this lifetime.

00:29:14.760 --> 00:29:28.840
Your mind already possesses the ability to touch every living being and promise it that you will care for it.

00:29:32.500 --> 00:29:36.700
The purpose of this Lam Rim,
the purpose of this retreat,

00:29:37.420 --> 00:29:40.160
is something like the journey to the center of the sun.

00:29:40.600 --> 00:29:43.000
Think of every living being.

00:29:43.360 --> 00:29:46.860
Countless living beings in a universe without limits.

00:29:48.320 --> 00:29:49.960
Meet them, one by one.

00:29:49.960 --> 00:29:51.420
Give each one, one by one, your promise.

00:29:52.220 --> 00:29:58.360
This is what happens during the first direct experience of bodhichitta.

00:29:58.360 --> 00:29:59.980
This really happens. This is what it feels like

00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:01.843
.

00:30:01.843 --> 00:30:05.340
If you keep visualizing it, it will help it to really happen.

00:30:06.000 --> 00:30:07.020
Really! So

00:30:07.020 --> 00:30:10.759
it is up to you,  If you truly want this,

00:30:11.340 --> 00:30:14.660
if you truly want to be a true Bodhisattva,

00:30:15.680 --> 00:30:22.220
then practice! Practice this visualization once or twice every day!

00:30:22.980 --> 00:30:28.140
Whenever you have a few minutes.
Just imagine it, in your mind's eye!

00:30:29.159 --> 00:30:32.989
And this will help it happen:
You will achieve Bodhichitta!

00:30:35.060 --> 00:30:43.120
And for such a Bodhisattva, something like the virus won't be a big deal at all.

00:30:43.120 --> 00:30:45.816
Just a tiny little thing!

00:30:45.820 --> 00:30:47.240
Earning money.

00:30:47.820 --> 00:30:49.360
Securing a livelihood.

00:30:49.600 --> 00:30:50.940
Feeding the family.

00:30:51.600 --> 00:30:53.600
Finding an apartment.

00:30:54.060 --> 00:30:58.660
All of these are unimaginable trifles. They are nothing!

00:31:00.240 --> 00:31:03.680
Your mind, your heart is like the center of the sun.

00:31:05.180 --> 00:31:15.120
And a few cookies, a few Coca-Colas at the center of the sun, that is truly meaningless.

00:31:16.380 --> 00:31:18.040
These things are not important.

00:31:18.560 --> 00:31:20.220
Strive for the big thing!

00:31:21.440 --> 00:31:23.662
Everything else is small in comparison.

00:31:23.662 --> 00:31:26.920
And then everything else will become effortless. Easy!

00:31:27.820 --> 00:31:29.820
That is Bodhichitta.

00:31:40.500 --> 00:31:43.220
See you in the next episode.

